110:- Older Pipeline ADRs (through ADR-0056) describe an eleven-step note producer/consumer taxonomy: extract, event_card_build, relevance_gate, verify_budget, impact_card_build, retrieve_graph_build, validate, retrieve, analyze, decide, review, split across an Dossier producer package and a Pipeline consumer half. The Feed cutover (ADR-0064, superseding ADR-0055/ADR-0056) deleted the Dossier package and the seven producer/impact/graph steps; current `STEP_ORDER` is exactly `retrieve -> analyze -> decide -> review`, reading Feed chunks directly. The Pipeline section must use current code as source of truth, not the older ADRs.
785:- the seven producer/impact/graph steps (`extract`, `event_card_build`, `relevance_gate`, `verify_budget`, `impact_card_build`, `retrieve_graph_build`, `validate`) and the `chunk` pre-step;
1022:Retrieve dispatches paired analyst sessions over Feed chunks, reading through the `feed_retrieve`/`feed_deref` tools (Feed contract v3). Current comments describe two paired sessions: Feed and Facts plus Technical and Market, and Fundamentals plus Sentiment. Retrieve builds an DossierPack whose themes cite `source_ref`s (chunk_ref/article_ref), uses market-data tools, surfaces contradictions, and emits analyst reports for Analyze. There is no note-graph walk, orphan-note scan, or `retrieve-graph-build` sidecar; the seven producer/graph steps that used to run before it (`extract` through `validate`, `impact_card_build`, `retrieve_graph_build`) are deleted (ADR-0064). Retrieval quality (coverage, independence) is computed off the step's own traced `feed_retrieve` calls (`computeRetrievalQuality`, `retrieve.ts:646`) and written onto `pack.retrieval_quality`, not derived from a note-graph theme count.

